<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
/** Public factual notice only. Never reads a session, connection, target or health record. */
function fitness_privacy_notice(): string {
 return '<h2 id="activity-data">Private activity and fitness data</h2><p>The optional Writer activity workspace is for the signed-in person’s own activity reports and personal targets. Google Health and Strava use separately authorised read connections. Samsung Health and Google Fit workout summaries can be selected through the Android Health Connect companion or a reviewed, mapped file. Connecting a general Google or Microsoft account does not authorise health access.</p>'
 .'<p>The workspace processes workout identifiers, source-app names, activity titles/types, times and available summary measurements such as active duration, distance and session steps. It does not request GPS routes, heart rate, sleep or clinical records. Health Connect history access is optional, checked for device support and requested only with separate user consent for longer reporting periods.</p>'
 .'<p>Cloud workout results are read on request and are not stored as an activity cache on this server. Provider identity and renewable access credentials are kept encrypted to maintain the selected connection. Reviewed file imports, personal targets and temporary import previews are encrypted in the private workspace and scoped to the signed-in Writer account. An import preview has a fifteen-minute confirmation window; expired previews are not used in reports. Saved imports can be replaced or deleted from the active workspace, and targets can be cleared for their calendar period.</p>'
 .'<p>Activity data is not sold, used for advertising, sent to AI tools or inserted into public articles, impact figures, newsletters or social posts. Reports are visible only in the corresponding private account. CSV downloads and printing/PDF are deliberate user actions. Files saved by the companion or downloaded to a device remain under that user’s control; deleting a website copy does not delete the provider’s records or files elsewhere.</p>'
 .'<p>The Android companion has no internet permission and does not upload automatically. Its exports use the document destination chosen by the user; a selected cloud-storage destination is operated by that storage provider. Health Connect permissions, including optional history, can be reviewed or revoked in Android settings.</p>'
 .'<p>Disconnecting in Writer removes local access credentials and attempts provider revocation. If remote revocation is not confirmed, the workspace states this and the user can remove the application in the provider’s settings. Google Health should use a dedicated Google Cloud project because Google revocation applies to all clients in the same project. Provider permissions, records and privacy controls remain subject to the provider’s own terms. Strava may collect API usage data under its <a href="https://www.strava.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.strava.com/legal/api_policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">API policy</a>.</p>';
}
